On Wed, May 29, 2013 at 10:43 PM, Robert LeChevalier <lojbab@lojban.org>wrote:

>
> betsemes
>> ...
>> xorxes
>>
>
> These are cmene
>
>  arxokuna
>> ...
>> tsani
>>
>
> These are brivla used as "nicknames".


I thougth that {betsemes}, {xorxes}, etc. were cmevla, not cmene.  My
understanding was that a cmene was everything that could be used as x1 of
{cmene} (which includes quoted brivla).
That said, {la} was a gadri meaning "the one/someone called ...." and that
was true regardless a cmevla or a brivla were used. After all many
languages (if not all) have proper nouns that also have a meaning in itself
(like "Fiore"->"Flower", "Bella"->"beautyful", "Remo"->"oar" for Italian).

Of course I might have been at fault for all this time.

This is why I would welcome the Merge. It would make rules about names
simpler.

remod

